From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: a WoW64 commit reports the Wine pages it committed

NtAllocateVirtualMemory(MEM_COMMIT) in an owner's i386 window rounded
the range out to 16 KiB host pages and returned that base. Windows
returns the 4 KiB page that holds the requested address. An unpacker
stub that maps its payload DLL itself (The Binding of Isaac: Rebirth,
The Witcher 2) commits each section at base + VirtualAddress and copies
the section to the address the commit returns: .text at base + 0x1000
came back as base, so the copy overwrote the headers whose section
table the stub was still walking. The next "section" then had code
bytes for its VirtualAddress and PointerToRawData, its commit failed
with STATUS_CONFLICTING_ADDRESSES and the copy read from
buffer + 0x7d8b5756, in the reserved upper half of the window:
c0000005 before the game's first line.

A commit now covers and reports whole Wine pages. The host-page
protection is already the union of each host page's Wine pages
(ios_wow64_apply_protection), as for NtProtectVirtualMemory and the
decommit; reserve keeps its 64 KiB base and host-page extent.

Linear: PLA-31, PLA-478

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-11-02-wow64-commit-pages.md
Offered-upstream: no; owner-local WoW64 VM is Playport code
---
 build/ntdll-unix/wow64_vm.h | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/wow64_vm.h b/build/ntdll-unix/wow64_vm.h
index 7a1b297..f5dbf38 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/wow64_vm.h
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/wow64_vm.h
@@ -84,6 +84,13 @@ static NTSTATUS ios_wow64_vm_allocate( uintptr_t window, void **addr, size_t *si
     }
     else
     {
+        /* Commit whole Wine (4 KiB) pages and report them, as Windows does: a PE
+         * loader copies each section to the address its commit returns, and a
+         * 16 KiB-rounded one put .text over the headers it was still reading.
+         * ios_wow64_apply_protection keeps a shared host page's neighbours. */
+        uintptr_t value = (uintptr_t)*addr;
+        base = (void *)(value & ~(uintptr_t)page_mask);
+        length = (*size + (value - (uintptr_t)base) + page_mask) & ~page_mask;
         view = find_view( base, length );
         if (!view || !(view->protect & VPROT_WOW64_VM)) return STATUS_CONFLICTING_ADDRESSES;
         status = ios_wow64_apply_protection( view, base, length, vprot | VPROT_COMMITTED );
-- 
